== Notes ==
{{Bug|The capture areas for Rooster's Challenge lag behind the indicated areas by the length of a radius. This is easily seen if you test positioning alone within (and outside) the circle.}}
* [[Mount]]s are disabled in the area. However, [[glider]]s are allowed.
* Players will be upscaled to level 80 while in the Celestial Challenge if they are not level 80 already.
* Players can exit to Divinity's Reach 
** By using the [[Invitation to Lunar New Year]].
** By interacting with the [[Exit the Celestial Challenge]] portal at the south end of the area or clicking it's icon on the map.
** By using a [[waypoint]] outside the area.
* Volunteering to a different instance will remove all stacks of Lucky Aura as if leaving the map.
* Players need to complete at least 4 challenge events to finish one round of the Celestial Challenge.
* During Dragon's or Rabbit's Challenge players do not take falling damage.
* Defeating foes can contribute to [[Slayer]] achievements, seemingly according to the default (non-Celestial) foe type.
* Enemies do not drop loot, but can trigger items like [[Jade Bot]] [[Module: Sensory Array|Scavenger Protocol]]s.
* You will be automatically revived when defeated, with the following message: {{red|Stay put! You will be revived soon.}}

== Trivia ==
* It is always day inside the instance.
* The player who contributes the most per challenge will be announced after a challenge is completed. Fireworks will also shoot up from under them.

